course: dictionary
lesson: 9228
title: Somewhere: a place you do not name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Somewhere means in, at or to a place, but it does not say exactly which place. «Keep your notebook somewhere private at home.» You know it is a place, but not which one. Look at the words around it to see what kind of place it is.
explain: Somewhere can also mean about, when you give a number. «The crowd was somewhere between 20 and 30 people.» The writer is not sure of the exact number, so somewhere shows it is a rough guess.
explain: The phrase «getting somewhere» means making progress. «We are getting somewhere with this puzzle» means we are finally moving forward. Ask yourself: is it a place, a rough number, or progress? The sentence tells you which.
fact: Somewhere means in, at or to a place, without saying exactly which one.
fact: When giving a number, somewhere means about or roughly, as in «somewhere around 50».
fact: «Getting somewhere» means making progress.
fact: «Somewhere» is the same as «someplace» in American English.
fact: In safety, if you go somewhere, tell an adult where you are going.
exercise: «The baker left the dough somewhere warm so it would rise.» What does somewhere mean here? | Very quickly | Making progress | Exactly at 10 o'clock | *In a warm place, not named exactly
exercise: «The crowd was somewhere between 20 and 30 people.» What does somewhere mean here? | Never | In a place called between | Exactly, with no doubt at all | *About, roughly
exercise: Dev says, «We are getting somewhere with this puzzle.» What does getting somewhere mean? | Getting lost in the rain | Going nowhere at all | Falling asleep | *Making progress
test: «Some people stay grumpy, so it is fine to play somewhere else.» What does somewhere else mean? | At a rough number | Very late at night | *In a different place | Inside the house
test: Why should you tell an adult where you are going, when you go somewhere new? | *So they know where to find you if you need help | To make the walk sound grown up | Because adults like lists | Because somewhere means yes
exam: In «Check it somewhere trusted», what does somewhere mean? | Sad and grumpy | Making progress | About trusted | *In a trusted place, not named exactly
